	(text "For C5:\nSince load is so small we don't need that much \nfiltering from the cap, and since we want this \nmodule to act like an LED replacement, the lamp may \nbe flashed or blinked so we don't actually want to \nstore too much charge\n\nCurrently RC = 0.1s and since the lamp effectively \nturns off when the output drops below ~63V, the \nactual turn-off time will be shorter than 5RC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 146.05 24.892 0)
